This plugin calls, by name and at runtime, skills it does not include:

- Matt Pocock's skills (https://github.com/mattpocock/skills), MIT licence.
  Nothing from that repository is copied here; the user installs it separately.
- Google's ADK skills (https://github.com/google/adk-python, .agents/skills/),
  Apache-2.0. Installed from Google's repository with the skills.sh installer;
  nothing from it is copied here.
- Matt Pocock's AI Coding Dictionary
  (https://github.com/mattpocock/dictionary-of-ai-coding). That repository
  states no licence. The persona links to its entries and reads them at
  runtime; nothing from it is copied here or into a target repository.

The baseline templates configure, but do not include, these tools in the
target repository:

- Repowise (https://github.com/repowise-dev/repowise), AGPL-3.0-or-later.
  Used as a development tool in CI and in a developer's shell only.
- ruff, mypy, import-linter, pylint, pytest, pre-commit, detect-secrets,
  bandit, mutmut, uv: each under its own licence.
